{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["And the verse's saying <b>they are the ones who speak</b> means — like a king who decrees upon his servant by a verbal order to do a thing. It further intends to inform you that even though you find the verse says that Moshe spoke, know that Aharon also spoke, as I will explain in the verse ״וַיְהִי בְּיוֹם דִּבֶּר ה׳״ (Exodus 6:28)." "<b>He is Moshe and Aharon.</b> Meaning, they are equal, and therefore sometimes Moshe is mentioned first and sometimes Aharon is mentioned first, and from this one can apply to the two of them a singular expression: ״he is Moshe and Aharon.״ Or perhaps the reason it said just before in the plural ״they are the ones who speak״ is because in the act of speaking they are distinct individuals."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:25:17.154085123Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}